            <p>Fall and winter reward the same habit: build the outfit in layers, in order, and let each layer do one job. The winter guide puts it plainly — a thin base layer, a warm middle layer, and a coat that actually closes over both, with shoes that handle cold ground. When any one of those layers fails, you spend the day either freezing or overheating, and the outfit stops mattering. Start there, and the rest of the season becomes a series of small choices rather than a daily guess.</p>
